-- title:
--   Embedding of H¹_S into the S-class group
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$ (as an element of `Nat.Primes`), and let $L$ be a finite-dimensional intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `IsUnramifiedOutside S`, i.e. $L$ is finite over $\mathbb{Q}$ and for every prime $q \notin S$ and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, the image in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ is contained in the fixing subgroup of $L$. The assertion is the existence of a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear map $f$ from the submodule `continuousH1Sr` of $H^1$ of the representation `sUnitsMaxRep S L`, taken with respect to the inclusion of $L$'s fixing subgroup into $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ — that is, the image under the projection `H1π` of the submodule of one-cocycles `levelCocyclesSr₁`, where `sUnitsMaxRep S L` is the subrepresentation of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}^{\times}$ (written additively) cut out by the subgroup `sUnitsMaxStable S L`, acted on by the fixing subgroup of $L$ — to `sClassGroupRep ↥L ↥L S`, the quotient of $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathcal{O}_L)$ (written additively, with its $L \simeq_{L} L$-action, hence trivially acted upon) by the submodule generated by the classes of primes lying over $S$, such that $f$ is injective and carries the $p$-torsion submodule of the source onto the full $p$-torsion submodule of this $S$-class group.
--
--   This is the injection of the $S$-ramified first cohomology of the $S$-units of the maximal $S$-ramified extension into the $S$-class group of $L$, obtained classically from inflation–restriction together with Hilbert's theorem 90 at each finite $S$-level, the cohomology group at a level being the capitulation kernel; the surjectivity onto $\mathrm{Cl}_S(L)[p]$ reflects that a $p$-torsion class capitulates in a Kummer extension which is again unramified outside $S$. It feeds the computation of the $H^2$ side with $\mu_p$-coefficients used by [`groupCohomology.finiteDimensional_and_nonempty_cyclotomicQuotientH2Rep_biprod_trivial_iso`](thm.html#groupCohomology.finiteDimensional_and_nonempty_cyclotomicQuotientH2Rep_biprod_trivial_iso).
